title: Heartland state Assembly referendum
subtitle: A petition for the dissolution of the state Assembly is launched.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1931 and month >= 3 and next_election_time_heartland - time >= 6 and marcher_heartland
on-arrival: landtag_ref_gold = 1 if gold_ideology == "Right" and gold_leader == "Coalfax" and not in_grand_coalition_heartland and not lvp_formed; liberal_cooperation -= 3 if landtag_ref_gold; strife += 1; pro_republic += gold_votes if not landtag_ref_gold; PLR_launched = 1
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/stahlhelm2.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= Heartland state Assembly referendum

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> has officially presented its plan for a referendum to dissolve the Assembly to Heartland Interior Minister Joshua Heath, aiming to strengthen the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> presence in the state Assembly, arguing that it no longer reflects the national mood. [? if not gallax_deported: Alaric Gallax’s?][? if gallax_deported: The?] <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> remains non-committal, [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": despite Mallin’s pleas, ?]dismissing the effort as a waste of resources for a government that will collapse within a year anyway.

For the petition to proceed to a plebiscite, it must gather signatures from over 20% of eligible voters—a significantly higher bar than the Serannus Plan referendum. Given the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>[? if not in_popular_front_heartland and not in_left_front_heartland:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>?]’s hesitation, success is far from guaranteed. [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": Furthermore, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, acting independently of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>, is not fully committed to the plan, arguing that a dissolution would primarily benefit the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> at their own expense. ?]

- @PLR_launched

@PLR_launched
title: The collection of signatures will begin next month.
on-arrival: political_decree_landtag = 1 if political_decree == 1

As we are in control of the democratic bulwark for now, we can attempt to use our position to our advantage.

- @campaign: Campaign against the referendum, and for democracy.
- @urge_paramilitary
- @hope: We have done enough.

@campaign
subtitle: -2 resources
view-if: not campaigned_democracy
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; pro_republic += 6; burgher_royalist -= pro_republic / 25; guild_royalist -= pro_republic / 25; commons_royalist -= pro_republic / 25; campaigned_democracy = 1
go-to: PLR_launched

We have campaigned against the referendum, but our success ultimately depends on the people's faith in democracy.

@urge_paramilitary
view-if: not political_decree_landtag and marcher_toleration
choose-if: marcher_heartland and strife >= 3 and unionist_relation >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not marcher_heartland: We don't control the Heartland government. ?] [? if strife < 3: Paramilitary violence isn't severe enough to justify an emergency decree. ?] [? if unionist_relation < 35: We lack sufficient relations with Askew. ?]
title: Urge Askew to grant us stronger actions against political extremists, and to restrict certain rights.
on-arrival: political_decree += 1; heartland_police_loyalty += 0.04; heartland_police_strength += 5; collectivist_relation -= 6; vanguard_militancy *= 0.9; vanguard_strength *= 0.85; loyalist_militancy *= 0.96; loyalist_strength *= 0.96; warden_militancy *= 0.98; warden_strength *= 0.98; commons_collectivist -= 1; commons_royalist -= 1; disfavored_collectivist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; burgher_royalist -= 2; dufour_angry_bruning += 5; political_decree_landtag = 1
go-to: PLR_launched

Joshua Heath and other Heartland officials have successfully urged Askew to issue an emergency decree expanding police authority to suppress political extremism. The decree imposes restrictions on political meetings, organizations, newspapers, and posters, all of which now require police approval beforehand.

As a result, several <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivist</span> newspapers have been banned, triggering violent clashes between their supporters and the police. [? if president == "DuFour": President DuFour has reluctantly signed the decree, but is losing patience with Askew for yielding to our demands. ?]

@hope

Hopefully a victory here could demoralize the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>.